{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfa5kixHsyYpVih8ucDbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The repair candidate `lapse_individual_balance_alternation` is written and passes the self-check. Whether it clears the novelty gate won't be known until admission, which is the one check the self-check doesn't run.\n\n**What went wrong before:** the rejected attempt added a streak penalty everyone shares to the incumbent. Every fit of that penalty so far has put its weight at about zero (0.04 ± 0.05 without the lapse, −0.004 ± 0.09 with it). So the model predicted almost exactly like the incumbent. Three other attempts this round (candidates 3 and 4 and their repairs) failed the novelty gate the same way.\n\n**The new model:** I refined `individual_balance_ideal_alternation`, the model statistically tied with the incumbent (16.0 ± 16.4 nats behind). Its fit shows a real balance effect: each person's weight on heads/tails imbalance averages 0.68 ± 0.37 and varies a lot between people (spread 1.9). The one change is adding the incumbent's rule that each person sometimes guesses instead of comparing, at their own rate. Guessing then accounts for the indifferent participants, so the alternation and balance preferences of engaged people can be as sharp as the data show. In alternation-matched pairs, the sequence with the shorter longest run is usually also the more balanced one. That is how this addresses the critique's streak-aversion discrepancy. No other slot this round has tried this combination.\n\n**Self-check:** it printed `OK`. It passed the import allowlist, the data contract and a short 1-chain fit, with a finite ELPD-LOO of −955.2 (the incumbent's is −973.3, but a smoke fit isn't directly comparable). Two warnings:\n- R-hat can't be computed from a single chain, so convergence isn't verified yet.\n- PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable: 5.5% of trials have high Pareto k, against a 1% tolerance. If the full fit still shows this, the model can't be exported as the winner even if it scores best.\n\nThe three files are in `experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_5_repair_1/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3845,"cache_read_input_tokens":75034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc83e546-0770-4250-b345-e2b04e5fc5b8","uuid":"de2bbb3d-6fc9-4e68-b9ff-061cd55a17a1","timestamp":"2026-09-30T18:17:31.824Z","request_id":"req_011Cfa5ki3U4rp3VjFSFGqQs"}
